        "code": "processing_gap",
        "reason": "processing_gap_178f1c4655c450df1e50: The source establishes caught-object identity, then string conversion, prefix formatting and printing in order. String conversion can fail before exception_text or error_message exists; later failure can occur after one or both intermediate values exist. The retained record incorrectly computes both values before its protected alternatives. The supplied vocabulary cannot faithfully replace that record while covering all four CFG outputs: case-local values cannot escape through ordinary output bindings, one protected group provides only one return port, and separate protected groups cannot repeatedly bind the same handler_exception output. A single protected group also cannot be partitioned among the three independently declared rendering and delivery actions. Precise identity, formatting and delivery operations are individually available, but their required conditional output availability is not expressible with these ports and scoping rules. A placeholder would retain the same availability defect or conceal the known print effect. This limitation concerns representation, not unknown exception contents; the latter remain a separate interface precision limitation.",
